      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Stopping the performance\" means letting go of the exhausting, self-imposed narrative that your worth is tied to a metric or a title. The pursuit was a habit, not a core identity; the *you* that chased the algorithms is just a temporary role you played. If the chase is gone, you are left with the quiet, unoptimized self—and that self deserves a different kind of attention, one that doesn't require constant, painful striving.",
      "source": "target",
